From: FF7 local performance investigation
Subject: [EXPERIMENT E04] drm/amdgpu: bounded same-BO multi-range PTE submission

Apply after E01 and E03 to the checksum-pinned CachyOS 7.2.8-1 source.
This private ABI is a native hardware experiment, not a stable userspace API.
Ordinary applications use their existing paths. The native-only adapter uses
GEM_VA operation 0xf704 with at most 16 ordinary 64-byte GEM_VA entries. Only
existing aligned 64 KiB VRAM mappings of the same VM-always-valid BO qualify.

Retain implicit unmap/movement dependencies, final completion/TLB handling and
DONT_PIPELINE. Form all leaf updates in one existing-size 1 KiB SDMA IB, and
commit once; reject overflow without submitting a partial batch. No chunk
GPU waits, pool enlargement or explicit-sync treatment is introduced.
EOPNOTSUPP is a pre-mutation eligibility rejection; other failures must not be
replayed by userspace. Correctness and performance on hardware remain untested.

